l four correct. 1/hbar_q = 10.0927, printed \"approx 10\", correct. Phi_q(0.989) = 671094 and Phi_q(1) = 901389 from the block's own product formula, printed \"6.7e5\" and \"9e5\", both correct. Jones polynomial of the trefoil -q^{-4}+q^{-3}+q^{-1} and Vol(trefoil) = 0, correct. All three ratio columns of the single-level table are internally consistent (0.911/1.165 = 0.782; -125.2/-89.8 = 1.394; 1.184/0.852 = 1.390) and CODATA n/p = 939.56542/938.27209 = 1.001378, printed 1.001, correct. TWO GENUINE DISCREPANCIES, both flagged not fixed: (1) The \"Descended vs transient\" table CONTRADICTS the block's own Statement display for its first row. The Statement asserts tr_M(Phi^trans) = Vol(K_beta)/hbar_q^2 - |tr_M(rho(beta))|. For the trefoil the block itself states Vol = 0, so that formula gives -0.551 - yet the table reports +111.86. The table value is instead Li_2(q^{-2})/hbar_q^2 = 111.8955 (the vacuum-drag mechanism the corpus uses for the volume-zero trefoil), so the row is right and the headline equation simply does not cover it. The block never says so. (2) The 4_1 row is off by 0.4%: Vol(4_1)/hbar_q^2 = 206.7683 and minus |tr_M| = 206.5863, against the printed 207.40; back-solving 207.40 + 0.182 implies Vol(4_1) = 2.03787 rather than 2.0298832. Minor third item: the ratio column reads 1137x where 207.40/0.182 = 1139.6 - consistent with the desc column being a rounding of ~0.18241, but not reproducible from the printed digits. Also note the tower table cannot discriminate the q_0 pins: proton and muon agree to well beyond the four printed figures.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:h00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"Voice","result":"fail","severity":"major","notes":"FIX IS SAFE BUT NOT APPLIED - the sentence sits between two math-bearing paragraphs and its removal is a judgement about how much scoping repetition the author wants, which the batch rules put on the structural side. Proposed: delete t